   ]
  },
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a571be6a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# EduAll: exploratory data analysis (EDA) helper notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "**Level 1 of computer-assisted decision making.** In this notebook the computer *describes* the whole cohort of 500 applicants: counts, distributions and comparisons. It does **not** read the applications for you, weigh criteria, or decide. You remain the one who interprets.\n",
    "\n",
    "Why use it? A human cannot hold 500 applicants × 44 variables (22,000 values) in mind at once. Summary statistics and plots compress the cohort into a few pictures you *can* reason about.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to use this notebook**\n",
    "1. Run the cells from top to bottom (`Shift + Enter`).\n",
    "2. The first cell downloads the EduAll repository from GitHub (github.com/AIforPhilanthropy/eduall), so no upload is needed.\n",
    "3. Answer the exercise questions in the empty cells. You may ask **Gemini** (side panel, or the Gemini prompt in an empty cell) to write code for you, but **read the code before running it** and check that the result makes sense.\n",
    "\n",
    "> Gemini writes code; the code computes. You can read and re-run every number. That is why EDA stays transparent even when an AI helps you type."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6e422f78",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 0. Load the data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7617ddb7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- Get the data -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "import os, pathlib, subprocess\n",
    "REPO_URL = \"https://github.com/AIforPhilanthropy/eduall.git\"\n",
    "NOTEBOOK_DIR = \".\"   # this notebook's folder inside the repository (change it if you move the notebook)\n",
    "here = pathlib.Path.cwd()\n",
    "if not any((p / \"data\" / \"EduAll_500_Applications_Dataset.csv\").exists() for p in [here, *here.parents]):\n",
    "    if not pathlib.Path(\"/content/eduall\").exists():\n",
    "        subprocess.run([\"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth\", \"1\", REPO_URL, \"/content/eduall\"], check=True)\n",
    "    os.chdir(pathlib.Path(\"/content/eduall\") / NOTEBOOK_DIR)\n",
    "print(\"working directory:\", os.getcwd())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "117448cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", 50)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find data/EduAll_500_Applications_Dataset.csv in this folder or a parent folder\n",
    "here = pathlib.Path.cwd()\n",
    "CSV = next(p / \"data\" / \"EduAll_500_Applications_Dataset.csv\" for p in [here, *here.parents]\n",
    "           if (p / \"data\" / \"EduAll_500_Applications_Dataset.csv\").exists())\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(CSV)\n",
    "print(f\"{df.shape[0]} applicants x {df.shape[1]} variables\")\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a0939aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1. Check the data before you trust it\n",
    "\n",
    "Key definitions (from the dataset summary):\n",
    "- `financial_need_chf` = **current monthly** shortfall: monthly expenses − family support − personal income (minimum 0). It does **not** deduct scholarships (per year) or savings (a stock).\n",
    "- `gni_tier`: income group of the country of origin (1 = lowest income, the Grant Call's priority countries).\n",
    "- `risk_*` and `resilience_*`: 0/1 flags from the declared circumstances.\n",
    "- `academic_standing = \"At Risk\"` means GPA below 2.5/4.0."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "58b88cd0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Variable types and missing values\n",
    "overview = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"type\": df.dtypes.astype(str),\n",
    "    \"missing\": df.isna().sum(),\n",
    "    \"unique values\": df.nunique(),\n",
    "})\n",
    "overview"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a240acc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2. Summary statistics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b052406b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Numeric variables: count, mean, spread, min, quartiles, max\n",
    "num_cols = [\"age\", \"gpa\", \"courses_completed\", \"semesters_in_program\",\n",
    "            \"monthly_expenses_chf\", \"family_income_chf\", \"personal_income_chf\",\n",
    "            \"savings_chf\", \"financial_need_chf\", \"external_scholarship_amount_chf\"]\n",
    "df[num_cols].describe().round(1).T"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b7620d92",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Categorical variables: how many applicants in each category?\n",
    "for col in [\"study_level\", \"gni_tier\", \"residency_permit\", \"study_mode\", \"academic_standing\"]:\n",
    "    print(df[col].value_counts().to_string(), \"\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "113febdb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Group summary: financial need by study level\n",
    "df.groupby(\"study_level\")[\"financial_need_chf\"].agg([\"count\", \"median\", \"mean\", \"min\", \"max\"]).round(0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "12d9bfad",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3. One variable at a time: distributions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "601cbb48",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "df[\"financial_need_chf\"].plot.hist(bins=30, ax=axes[0], color=\"#660033\")\n",
    "axes[0].set(title=\"Monthly financial need (CHF)\", xlabel=\"CHF per month\", ylabel=\"Applicants\")\n",
    "df[\"gpa\"].plot.hist(bins=25, ax=axes[1], color=\"#9A3B66\")\n",
    "axes[1].axvline(2.5, color=\"black\", linestyle=\"--\", label=\"Normal minimum 2.5\")\n",
    "axes[1].set(title=\"GPA (out of 4.0)\", xlabel=\"GPA\", ylabel=\"Applicants\")\n",
    "axes[1].legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2cee505e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "df[\"study_level\"].value_counts().plot.bar(ax=axes[0], color=\"#660033\", rot=0)\n",
    "axes[0].set(title=\"Applicants by study level\", ylabel=\"Applicants\")\n",
    "df[\"country_origin\"].value_counts().head(10).sort_values().plot.barh(ax=axes[1], color=\"#9A3B66\")\n",
    "axes[1].set(title=\"Top 10 countries of origin\", xlabel=\"Applicants\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6572eecf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4. Two variables and groups: relationships"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2fdc8b1a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4.5))\n",
    "levels = [\"Bachelor's\", \"Master's\", \"Doctoral\"]\n",
    "axes[0].boxplot([df.loc[df.study_level == l, \"financial_need_chf\"] for l in levels])\n",
    "axes[0].set_xticks([1, 2, 3], levels)\n",
    "axes[0].set(title=\"Monthly need by study level\", ylabel=\"CHF per month\")\n",
    "axes[1].scatter(df[\"gpa\"], df[\"financial_need_chf\"], s=12, alpha=0.5, color=\"#660033\")\n",
    "axes[1].set(title=\"GPA vs monthly need\", xlabel=\"GPA\", ylabel=\"CHF per month\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d466e77a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cross-table: income tier of the country of origin x study level\n",
    "pd.crosstab(df[\"gni_tier\"], df[\"study_level\"], margins=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c65231ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5. Derived indicators (your choices, made explicit)\n",
    "\n",
    "These columns are **illustrative**. Each one encodes a decision (what counts as risk, how many courses a degree needs). Change them if your group decides differently, and write down why."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b9bb0c70",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "risk_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith(\"risk_\")]\n",
    "res_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith(\"resilience_\")]\n",
    "df[\"n_risks\"] = df[risk_cols].sum(axis=1)\n",
    "df[\"n_resilience\"] = df[res_cols].sum(axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Courses still needed (Grant Call: bachelor 40, master 12, doctorate 12 courses)\n",
    "required = {\"Bachelor's\": 40, \"Master's\": 12, \"Doctoral\": 12}\n",
    "df[\"courses_remaining\"] = (df[\"study_level\"].map(required) - df[\"courses_completed\"]).clip(lower=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "df[[\"student_id\", \"n_risks\", \"n_resilience\", \"courses_remaining\"]].describe().round(2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1e86ee78",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# How common is each risk factor?\n",
    "df[risk_cols].mean().sort_values().mul(100).round(1).plot.barh(color=\"#660033\", figsize=(7, 4),\n",
    "    title=\"Share of applicants with each risk flag (%)\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"% of applicants\"); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7214516a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6. \"What if\" pools: how big is the group a rule would select?\n",
    "\n",
    "This is still EDA: you state a rule, the computer counts exactly. It does not tell you whether the rule is fair or wise."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "314a4058",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def pool(mask, label):\n",
    "    sub = df[mask]\n",
    "    print(f\"{label}: {len(sub)} applicants \"\n",
    "          f\"({len(sub)/len(df):.0%}); total monthly need CHF {sub.financial_need_chf.sum():,.0f}\")\n",
    "    return sub.groupby(\"study_level\").size().rename(\"applicants\")\n",
    "\n",
    "pool((df.gpa >= 2.5) & (df.financial_need_chf > 0), \"GPA >= 2.5 and positive need\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "711a952e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Try your own rule, e.g. priority countries with at least two risk flags:\n",
    "pool((df.gni_tier == 1) & (df.n_risks >= 2), \"GNI tier 1 and 2+ risk flags\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6b421612",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Exercises\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer each question with code (yours or Gemini's) and write one sentence of interpretation.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. How many applicants report **zero** monthly need? What could explain a zero?\n",
    "2. How does the median monthly need differ between bachelor's, master's and doctoral applicants?\n",
    "3. What share of applicants come from **GNI tier 1** countries?\n",
    "4. How many applicants are **\"At Risk\"** academically, and how does their need compare with the others?\n",
    "5. The budget is CHF 500,000 per year. Compare it with the cohort's total monthly need × 12. What does the gap mean for your allocation?\n",
    "6. Which plot surprised you most, and which question does it raise that the numbers alone cannot answer?"
   ]
  },
