   "source": [
    "## Prompting Gemini well\n",
    "\n",
    "Weak: *\"make a plot\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Strong: *\"Using the dataframe `df`, draw a box plot of `financial_need_chf` grouped by `study_level`, with the y-axis labelled CHF per month.\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Checklist before you trust an AI-written cell:\n",
    "- Does the code use the **right column**? (`financial_need_chf` is monthly!)\n",
    "- Does the number of rows match what you expect (500, or the size of your filter)?\n",
    "- Re-run the cell: does it give the same result?\n",
    "- If there is an error, use **Explain error**, then read the fix before accepting it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "95d516c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What EDA cannot do\n",
    "\n",
    "EDA shows the shape of the cohort, data problems and the size of candidate pools. It cannot read 500 personal statements, judge credibility, or tell you what is fair. That is where the next step (AnythingLLM) and, above all, your judgement come in."
   ]
  }
